\b 1. Permission\b0\par
You may install and use InputBridge on your own Windows devices. You may copy and redistribute the original installer as long as you do not modify it or misrepresent its source.\par
\par
\b 2. Purpose\b0\par
InputBridge is a local input bridge that allows a phone browser on the same network to send text input to the current cursor position on a Windows computer.\par
\par
\b 3. Network and Input Access\b0\par
InputBridge starts a local network service and listens on the configured port. Anyone who can access the displayed address may be able to send input to your computer. Use it only on trusted networks and close the application when you do not need it.\par
\par
\b 4. Privacy\b0\par
InputBridge is designed for local use. Input content is transmitted between your phone browser and your computer over your local network. The software does not intentionally upload your input content to a remote server.\par
